<LegalDoc
  title="Subscription Terms"
  description="The commercial terms for paid TaskForce subscriptions — pricing, billing, renewal and cancellation. A working draft, pending final legal review."
  eyebrow="Legal & Trust"
  updated="31 July 2026"
  draft={true}
>
  <p>
    These Subscription Terms cover paid TaskForce plans, and complement our
    <a href="/legal/terms">Terms of Service</a>. They are written for business customers. Placeholders
    in <code>[brackets]</code> mark details we'll confirm before launch.
  </p>

  <h2>Plans & pricing</h2>
  <p>
    Plans, limits and what's included are described on the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a>. Prices
    are shown <strong>excluding VAT</strong> and in <strong>euros (EUR)</strong>; applicable taxes are
    added at checkout. <strong>(Prices are indicative until launch.)</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>AI usage</h2>
  <p>
    AI features are metered by consumption (tokens) across the plans that include them. Where you run
    local models, that usage stays on your own infrastructure. Overage and fair-use limits are described
    on the pricing page.
  </p>

  <h2>Billing & renewal</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Subscriptions are billed in advance, <strong>monthly or annually</strong>, through our payment provider.</li>
    <li>Unless cancelled, a subscription <strong>renews automatically</strong> for the same period.</li>
    <li>Per-seat plans are billed for the seats in use; adding seats is prorated.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cancellation</h2>
  <p>
    You can cancel at any time from your workspace settings or by contacting us. Cancellation stops the
    next renewal; access continues until the end of the paid period. Fees already paid are
    non-refundable except where required by law.
  </p>

  <h2>Right of withdrawal</h2>
  <p>
    Business customers generally do not benefit from the consumer 14-day right of withdrawal. Where a
    subscriber qualifies as a consumer, the statutory withdrawal right applies as required by law.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes, suspension & termination</h2>
  <p>
    We may change plan pricing or contents with reasonable notice, effective at your next renewal. We may
    suspend or terminate a subscription for non-payment or a material breach of the
    <a href="/legal/terms">Terms of Service</a>. On termination you can export your data for a reasonable
    period — see the <a href="/legal/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of <strong>France</strong>, without prejudice to
    mandatory consumer protections.
  </p>
</LegalDoc>
